+### Bottleneck Breakdown in `spec/requests` (StackProf + RSpecDissect)
+
+1. **Global `Sidekiq.testing!(:inline)` (~30% / ~42s of post-Phase-1 140s run)**
+   - `TriggerWebhookWorker#perform`: **30.4s (21.9%)**
+   - `LocalNotificationWorker#perform`: **5.4s (3.9%)**
+   - `ActionMailer::MailDeliveryJob#perform` (including `Premailer` CSS inlining): **5.0s (3.6%)**
+   - `DistributionWorker#perform`: **4.5s (3.3%)**
+   - Out of 263 request spec files (1,877 examples), only **9 files** genuinely needed inline Sidekiq execution (3 email assertions including 1 negative `capture_emails` check, `UnfavouriteWorker`, `DistributionWorker` for home timeline & direct conversations, and `LocalNotificationWorker` for notification setup).
+
+2. **Repeated route clearing & reloading (~6.7s / 4.8% of 140s run)**
+   - `spec/requests/signature_verification_spec.rb` called `Rails.application.routes.draw` in `before` and `Rails.application.reload_routes!` in `after` across all **30 examples**, consuming **6.7s** in `ActionDispatch::Routing::RouteSet::NamedRouteCollection#define_url_helper` / `#clear!`.
+
+3. **Repeated OAuth user + access token fabrication in shared API auth context (~8–9s across 70+ files)**
+   - `spec/support/api_authentication.rb` (`shared_context 'with API authentication'`, included in 70+ request specs) fabricated a fresh `:user` / `:admin_user` (BCrypt + Account + 2 LoginActivity) and `:accessible_access_token` on every example (**6.5s**).
+   - `spec/support/examples/api.rb` (`shared_examples 'forbidden for wrong role'`, called **73 times** across 14 admin specs) fabricated another brand-new `:user` and `:accessible_access_token` on every call (~1.0s).
+
+4. **`Premailer::Rails::Hook` CSS inlining in tests (~2.1s in `spec/requests`, larger in `spec/mailers`)**
+   - `Premailer::Adapter::Nokogiri#to_inline_css` parsed the full compiled mailer CSS and executed Nokogiri XPath queries on every delivered HTML email (~350ms per email). No spec in the suite tests Premailer CSS inlining.
+
+5. **`Rack::Attack` middleware running on every request (~1.15s across all 263 files)**
+   - `Rack::Attack#call` executed `blocklisted?` (0.74s) and `throttled?` (0.40s — including redundant `Doorkeeper::OAuth::Token.authenticate` queries and Redis/cache lookups) on every HTTP request in all 263 request specs, even though only `spec/config/initializers/rack/attack_spec.rb` tests `Rack::Attack`.
+
+6. **Repeated immutable setup in heavy request specs (`RSpecDissect`: 109.8s -> 24.9s)**
+   - `spec/requests/cache_spec.rb`: **26.95s** (post-Sidekiq 22.94s) recreating alice, moderator user, 2 statuses, invite, poll, token, and follow across **258 read-only GET examples**! Converting one `before` -> `before_all` dropped it to **3.6–4.2s**.
+   - `spec/requests/activitypub/replies_spec.rb`: **12.2s** (post-Sidekiq 7.65s) creating 7 statuses per example across **45 examples** -> **1.7s**.
+   - `spec/requests/api/v1/notifications_spec.rb`, `v2/notifications_spec.rb`, `v2/notifications/accounts_spec.rb`: **14s combined** running 6 services + inline Sidekiq on every example -> **~1.6s combined**.
+   - `spec/requests/activitypub/contexts_spec.rb`: `GET #show` pagination context forgot `stub_const 'ActivityPub::ContextsController::DESCENDANTS_LIMIT', 2` (already used in `GET #items` in the same file), fabricating 40 statuses unnecessarily -> **1.76s -> 0.33s**.
